{"title":"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product of two positive numbers is 9. The reciprocal of one of these numbers is 4 times the reciprocal of the other number. What is the sum of the two numbers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d845a6293555ff25411b727306dbc36e6111e506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{10}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{20}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{15}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"388\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the two numbers equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. From the information given in the problem, two equations can be written:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f0457561f9f1b01411cfbe364647dd0eac1b1ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c86dd577c0eae94254c0707bb909c9f742af2ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x}=4 \\left( \\frac{1}{y} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"87\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c8e5841ffebe81e4f0a4ca06c1500abf637dc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> in the equation,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab7ab1cff4fed46c3ebb0cf7b06d3ba86db40b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b469dcc2e054456ab4c6d9a8c8b5403a61178241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/96833e93d4751aed0ef00575b813c588e9645200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a90dec76e5e58db01806005f31c9be903a11c194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0adfad30accea7db26a323c1116bffc3b6193bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2}+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0eb0750a713be53278f8fcd44d18edcb0cafa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{15}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set up your first equation which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f0457561f9f1b01411cfbe364647dd0eac1b1ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> and your second being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3b0afe9ba93c146c4313ff2130f4d38d36e884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{x} = \\dfrac4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"54\" height=\"42\" />. Then, in the first equation, rearrange it to become <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232764b740b5ee19b9eaa069dd6404f3a4340608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac9y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"50\" height=\"42\" />. Now plug this in to your second equation, and you should get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18b8aeb6594aa7ff842d9121a2ea1879bdb2ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{y}{9}=\\dfrac{4}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"53\" height=\"42\" />. Cross multiply to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7dbdc10663e613dbc7432d02bb6e7d80cc4262bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, and simplify to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daaf07d9f0a2413768e291d1264b59b3c835e4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. Notice how the problem mentioned that they were positive integers, so we don't consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3683f227b0b53e6a30087db2fa3b752965ecf05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. We plug <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> back into our first equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fca98ed95e07ce6a6a0f88bb9de83dde2e2f4b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> which makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> come out to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />. We add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac10c3108aa384a5f230659767b1866aa2437ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=6+1.5=7.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"17\" />. Notice answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the only fraction that simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15788e198a53ced87268aea78fcde68a84de92c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, so answer option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" /> must be the answer.\n</p><p>~bhargchi\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jyA5_tjDOjc\">https://youtu.be/jyA5_tjDOjc</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A\">2012 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2012 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145934\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 251/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2320/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5461/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.699      1 -total\n 63.60%    9.985      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 35.43%    5.562      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key